        {
            "id": "https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45309",
            "content_html": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">MDN URL</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ProcessingInstruction\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ProcessingInstruction</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What specific section or headline is this issue about?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Description</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What information was incorrect, unhelpful, or incomplete?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We should consider moving/duplicating some of this data to a Processing Instructions guide rather than only having this under the <code class=\"notranslate\">api</code> page.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is especially relevant with Processing Instructions becoming more of a thing in HTML as part of Chrome's Declarative Partial Updates: <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/declarative-partial-updates#out-of-order_streaming\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/declarative-partial-updates#out-of-order_streaming</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also the discussion here: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5204758205\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/30292\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30292/hovercard?comment_id=5409628333&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30292#issuecomment-5409628333\">mdn/browser-compat-data#30292 (comment)</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What did you expect to see?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A separate Processing Instructions guide.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Do you have any supporting links, references, or citations?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Do you have anything more you want to share?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45309",
            "title": "[dom] Add Processing Instructions guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-25T11:33:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "id": "https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43568",
            "content_html": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">MDN URL</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What specific section or headline is this issue about?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What information was incorrect, unhelpful, or incomplete?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event\" rel=\"nofollow\">Element: input event</a> page has the following breadcrumbs:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web APIs</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element\" rel=\"nofollow\">Element</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/input_event\" rel=\"nofollow\">input</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This confused me a bit, because <code class=\"notranslate\">input</code> is also <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/input\" rel=\"nofollow\">an HTML <em>element</em></a>, which has the following breadcrumbs:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML\" rel=\"nofollow\">HTML</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference\" rel=\"nofollow\">Reference</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements\" rel=\"nofollow\">Elements</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/input\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;input&gt;</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">What did you expect to see?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I would expect the breadcrumb leaf for the event page to has an indicator, such as \"input event\" or \"input (event)\".</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Do you have any supporting links, references, or citations?</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Do you have anything more you want to share?</h3>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/495429/568506780-11ec2595-308d-4a1a-9a0b-56fe1ae2d9c2.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTMzOTA1MTcsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzM5MDIxNywicGF0aCI6Ii80OTU0MjkvNTY4NTA2NzgwLTExZWMyNTk1LTMwOGQtNGExYS05YTBiLTU2ZmUxYWUyZDljMi5wbmc_.E1aWyAsayWeJcDNsTiRzb79isE3hbxPEEhJS9pbOj7o\"><img width=\"898\" height=\"85\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/495429/568506780-11ec2595-308d-4a1a-9a0b-56fe1ae2d9c2.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTMzOTA1MTcsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzM5MDIxNywicGF0aCI6Ii80OTU0MjkvNTY4NTA2NzgwLTExZWMyNTk1LTMwOGQtNGExYS05YTBiLTU2ZmUxYWUyZDljMi5wbmc_.E1aWyAsayWeJcDNsTiRzb79isE3hbxPEEhJS9pbOj7o\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 85px;; aspect-ratio: 898 / 85; background-color: var(--bgColor-muted); border-radius: 6px\" class=\"js-gh-image-fallback\"></a>",
